[Music]  it is national consumer protection week  here's a look at several common schemes  what to do if you suspect a scam or have  become the victim of a scammer  scammers are always coming up with new  ways to try to get our money bernard  bermudez managed to avoid becoming the  victim of one recently thanks to a  conscientious uber driver i hopped into  the uber car  and the um the driver told me to put a  pin number  and he asked me for a pin i'm gonna go  what pin number and so i had to put in a  pin number and he had to match it up on  his phone i asked him why did they do  that and he said to me that there's a  lot of fraud going on with the uber  space and  maybe 20 seconds after that happened  somebody pinged him pretending he was me  bermudez is also a vice president with  enterprise bank and trust here in las  vegas he says common scams they're  seeing include phony usps text messages  citing a reason for a missed delivery  directing the person to a website to pay  for a re-delivery and the card  information is then stolen bermuda says  the scam is often used during tax refund  season if you are expecting a delivery  call or stop by your local post office  instead and don't trust a text  another common scam travel sites with  the property listed for rent where a  person asked to be paid outside of the  system to avoid fees never pay for  services outside the system because you  will have a more difficult time  recovering your money  if and when something goes wrong and  also if you get an email or a text  message from your bank or your credit  card company or anyone asking you to do  something pick up the phone and call the  bank's telephone number do not call back  to the number that sent you the text  if you suspect a scam call the ftc the  federal trade commission is the main  agency that collects scam reports and if  you think you have become a victim of  fraud report potentially compromised  bank account credit or debit card  information to your financial  institutions immediately

